# FS-UAE SLIRP: the DNS forwarder is 10.0.2.3.  The GATEWAY is 10.0.2.2 and it
# does NOT answer DNS -- this file said 10.0.2.2 until 2026-07-25, and every
# on-Amiga name lookup in the tree was paying for it:
#
#   nameserver 10.0.2.2    gethostbyname("example.com")   30.06 s
#   nameserver 10.0.2.3    gethostbyname("example.com")    0.58 s
#
# Measured from a program linked against nothing of ours, on the 14 MHz A1200
# profile, same boot image, only this line changed.  The lookups SUCCEEDED
# either way, which is why nobody noticed: DHCP supplies a working server as
# well, so the resolver waits out 10.0.2.2, falls back, and answers -- thirty
# seconds late.  fetch, host, tests/tls/run-fetch.sh and every conformance DNS
# case were all paying it, and no harness timed a single command.
#
# The thirty seconds is the resolver's own failover time and is worth a look
# on its own account; see docs/RESEARCH.md.
nameserver 10.0.2.3
domain localdomain
